  "note": "The ack ledger's original revocation time (host-work-v1 section 11.4; Atem's proposal, for Astation's agreement, #120 comment 7234876179). A Station that starts late or reads a legacy row records its own revoke of svc-discord, covering host-b and host-c, with no authenticated original time (no revoked_at_ms): the start is the revoke's issued_at, at or after the revocation (the Station signs its own revoke only once the Portal revoked), so its final comes at issued_at + 24 h and nothing 1 ms before (a branch: another history from the committed state). A start may be late, never early: deadline_passed says every task admitted before the revocation has passed its deadline. A learn before any own revoke is refused unknown_revocation. host-b applies it, and the Station restarts before it learns the Portal's original time (learn_revoked_at), which only lowers the start: a later date changes nothing; a date 2 h earlier moves the deadline 2 h earlier with nothing at once (two replicas: the one that lost makes nothing; the same date again changes nothing; a branch shows the final 2 h earlier); two learns give the same ledger in either order; a date 25 h earlier ends the window: the final at once, revoked{deadline_passed, pending_hosts: [host-c]}, after host-b's report made before it. A date learned after the final, earlier still, lowers the stored start but makes no report and changes neither a report nor the final (the final stands and is made once), so two dates that would each end the window give the same ledger in either order (a branch); a later one changes nothing. host-c applies it later: its revocation_applied is still made and sent after the final. The reports and their ids are the deadline fixture's: only the final's time moved, and only earlier.",
